  "about": "The tune is Tempus adest floridum, a spring carol from the 13th century. It was first published in 1582 in Piae Cantiones, a Finnish song book. In 1853 the English hymnwriter John Mason Neale wrote new words to it, with his music editor Thomas Helmore. The carol tells of a king of Bohemia who braves the winter weather to give alms to a poor peasant.",
